 *   **Time Complexity:** Octree build time is bounded by CPU performance. For a $512^3$ volume (256MB), building octrees took 6.5ms on a Xeon 1.7GHz and 3.5ms on a Xeon 3.0GHz [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** Depends on brick size and available texture memory. Smaller bricks increase overlap overhead; larger bricks require more texture memory [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Performance:** Significant acceleration is achieved over non-optimized GPU rendering.
-    *   QuadroFX 3400: 73.5 fps (optimized) vs 9.6 fps (non-optimized), 7.66x acceleration [S1, unofficial].
-    *   ATi FireGL X1 (xy aligned): 83.3 fps (optimized) vs 0.23 fps (non-optimized), 362x acceleration [S1, unofficial].
-    *   ATi FireGL X1 (non xy aligned): 27.4 fps (optimized) vs 0.23 fps (non-optimized), 119x acceleration [S1, unofficial].
-    *   3DLabs Wildcat 7110: 21.3 fps (optimized) vs 0.38 fps (non-optimized), 56.1x acceleration [S1, unofficial].
